        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(plugin-sdk): keep approval slugs UTF-16-safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nApproval slugs are short channel-facing prefixes derived from approval IDs. Several builders produced them with `id.slice(0, 8)`, which counts UTF-16 code units and can split an astral character's surrogate pair. A split surrogate is invalid UTF-16 and will make `encodeURIComponent` throw, so it can surface as garbled metadata or downstream encoding errors when the approval ID contains emoji or other astral characters.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced the raw `slice(0, 8)` calls with `truncateUtf16Safe(..., 8)`, the existing surrogate-aware helper from `@openclaw/normalization-core/utf16-slice`. This keeps the same 8-character budget while refusing to cut a surrogate pair in half.\n\n## User Impact\n\nApproval prompts and reaction metadata that derive slugs from plugin/exec approval IDs now stay well-formed when the ID lands on a surrogate boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `src/plugin-sdk/approval-renderers.ts`: `buildPluginApprovalPendingReplyPayload`, `buildTypedPluginApprovalPendingReplyPayload`, and `buildPluginApprovalResolvedReplyPayload` now truncate with `truncateUtf16Safe`.\n- `src/plugin-sdk/approval-reaction-runtime.ts`: `buildMetadataPayload` and the exec fallback in `buildApprovalReactionPendingContent` now truncate with `truncateUtf16Safe`.\n- Regression tests in `approval-renderers.test.ts` and `approval-reaction-runtime.test.ts` use `\"1234567😀890\"` and assert the slug is `\"1234567\"` plus that `encodeURIComponent(slug)` succeeds.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Test command:\n  ```bash\n  pnpm test src/plugin-sdk/approval-renderers.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/approval-reaction-runtime.test.ts\n  ```\n- Output:\n  ```\n   Test Files  2 passed (2)\n        Tests  25 passed (25)\n     Duration  4.01s\n  ```\n- Before behavior: `\"1234567😀890\".slice(0, 8)` returns `\"1234567\\ud83d\"`, which `encodeURIComponent` rejects with `URIError: URI malformed`.\n- After behavior: `truncateUtf16Safe(\"1234567😀890\", 8)` returns `\"1234567\"`, and `encodeURIComponent` succeeds.\n",
        "branch": "fix/approval-slug-utf16",
